      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:2:31:3",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ الصَّبِيِّ يُزَوَّجُ الصَّبِيَّةَ هَلْ يَتَوَارَثَانِ قَالَ إِذَا كَانَ أَبَوَاهُمَا [هُمَا] اللَّذَانِ زَوَّجَاهُمَا فَنَعَمْ قُلْتُ أَ يَجُوزُ طَلَاقُ الْأَبِ قَالَ لَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ibn Fazal, from Al Qasim Bin Urwa, from Ibn Bakeyr, from Ubeyd Bin Zurara, ",
          "The narrator says: ‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about the young boy who marries the young girl (both immature), would they both be inheriting?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘If their fathers who were the ones who arranged their marriage, then yes’. I said, ‘Is the divorce by the father permissible?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘No’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from ibn Faddal from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Urwah from ibn Bukayr from ‘Ubayd ibn Zurarah who has narrated the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the case of a child who marries a female child; if they inherit each other. He (the Imam) said, ‘If their fathers are the ones who have arranged their marriage then they inherit.’ I then asked, ‘Is their divorce by father permissible?’ He (the Imam) said, ‘No, it is not permissible.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
